title: Settings › Pause › Pause one agent, resume all
route: /settings
intro: Each row has its own switch. The header button and banner follow the switches: they show 'paused' only when all sixteen are off. This is how the page behaves for one, a few, or all switches.
dir: TD
also: Tested in the built demo. The switch has no label and no toast. The only sign of a single pause is the switch itself.
---
screen s1 "Settings\nAll sixteen switches on. Header button reads 'Pause all agents'"
click c1 "Click a row's switch\nNo label, no confirmation"
decision q1 "Was the switch on?"
store a1 "That agent is paused\nSwitch goes grey, no toast, the row text does not change"
store a2 "That agent is active again\nSwitch goes green, no toast"
decision q2 "Are all sixteen switches now off?"
process b1 "Header button stays 'Pause all agents'\nNo banner"
process b2 "Header button becomes 'Resume all agents'\nAmber banner 'All agents are paused' appears"
decision q3 "Were all sixteen off before this click?"
process b3 "Banner goes and the button returns to 'Pause all agents'\nThe other fifteen stay paused"
toast m1 "With one to fifteen off there is no 'Resume all agents' button\nTurn each switch on, or use 'Pause all agents' then 'Resume all agents'"
click c2 "Click 'Pause all agents' while some are off"
goto g1 "Continues in: Settings › Pause › Pause all agents"
click c3 "Click 'Resume all agents'\nOnly shown when all sixteen are off"
store d1 "All sixteen switches go on"
toast d2 "'Agents resumed'\nGreen toast"
end e1 "Page is back to normal"

s1 --> c1 --> q1
q1 -->|Yes| a1 --> q2
q1 -->|No| a2 --> q3
q2 -->|No| b1 --> m1
q2 -->|Yes| b2
q3 -->|Yes| b3 --> m1
q3 -->|No| b1
m1 --> c2 --> g1
b2 --> c3 --> d1 & d2
d1 --> e1
d2 --> e1
